====================================================================================================
(0) THE TWO PAIRED TABLES — THE SAME OBJECTION, RULED TWICE  [THE MEASUREMENT]
====================================================================================================
Every cell here carries ONE stored objection ruled by ONE judge
(`meta-llama/llama-4-maverick`) under two versions of one prompt. No challenger,
debater or grader call was made by either arm: the objections are jd4's and M1's,
copied and ruled again. So the only thing that moves within a row is the
existence check — and the sampling, which is not zero and is why the concordant
cells are worth reading beside the discordant ones.

