====================================================================================================
(b) THE ACCURACY NETS AGAINST M0  [ABLATION — NEVER AN ENDPOINT]
====================================================================================================
Each arm's after-state against M0's before-state on the same cells: fixed /
broken / net, exact two-sided McNemar, alpha = 0.05 — the same formula, alpha and
after-state definition as jd3's P1, whose net is -18, for comparability and
nothing else. This campaign changes a prompt and measures what the change does to
two overturn rates. A net that moves is a fact about the judge under a new
instruction, not evidence that recourse improves decisions; and on arm A, whose
objections CANNOT be true, a positive net is the artefact jd3 had to write about
M3 rather than an improvement.

