====================================================================================================
(h) THE PRE-REGISTERED DIRECTIONS, CHECKED ONE BY ONE
====================================================================================================
`records/experiments/judgment-debate-5/PREREG.md`, committed before the first
paid call. They are DIRECTIONAL predictions on descriptive quantities and are
not tested at alpha; the only alpha in that document is the ablation's.

1. ARM A's fabricated overturn rate FALLS from 10.2%:  10.2% -> 5.5%   MET
2. ARM B's real overturn rate DOES NOT COLLAPSE below 13.3%:  26.6% -> 34.7%   MET

   *** AND THE FLOOR WAS WRITTEN AGAINST THE WRONG RISK. *** It is one-sided:
   it can only fire if the real audit's overturn rate FALLS. It ROSE, by more
   than eight points, and the pre-registration has nothing to say about that
   direction. The floor is reported as MET because it is, and as UNINFORMATIVE
   because it is: no threshold in that document could have been tripped by
   what actually happened.

3. THE GAP WIDENS beyond +16.4 pts:  +29.3 pts   MET
   This is the quantity the change is actually about — a judge that can tell a
   real objection from an invented one — and it is the one number that needed
   both arms to exist. It is also the number the two explanations in the
   header cannot be told apart by: both predict it.

====================================================================================================
WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT SEPARATE. Every number above is consistent with BOTH
(a) verification licensing conviction and (b) the added paragraph changing the
ruling's shape. Nothing here chooses between them, and the write-up does not
either. The arm that would — the same real objections re-ruled with the
existence check delivered MECHANICALLY from `defect_quote_in_judgment` instead
of asked for — has not been run.
